+   * it — a project pinned to the old version would get whatever the first
+   * importer loaded. A tree per digest gives each version its own path, so two
+   * versions can be live at once and neither is a guess.
+   *
+   * The tree is derived data: it is built from the blobs, verified against the
+   * digest it claims to be, and can be deleted and rebuilt at any time. What it
+   * does NOT carry is file modes — the listing covers bytes and link targets,
+   * not permissions — so a materialised tree is byte-identical and
+   * metadata-approximate, which is stated here rather than discovered later.
+   */
